P1 (aarch64, gen 32): **the thread finaliser footprint without the VCPU-link words** (namespace `K8`, the
continuation of QueueFoot8), generated by `proofs/scratch/a64/g32/gen8.py` from `proofs/scratch/a64/g32/cone.out`
(run 3: the cone of `fin_thread.blk`, 117 constants, without the constants QueueFoot8 already copies). Not edited
by hand. Same transformation as QueueFoot8 (`192` → `224`, the TCB clause without offsets 3664 / 3672, namespace
`K8`, `kw` / `kwB` → `kw8` / `kwB8`).

Every side goal closed by the original tactic: after `vcpu::detach`, the thread finalisation (`unbind_notification`,
`timer::remove`, `unbind_tcb`, `complete_yield_to`, `suspend`, `debug_remove`) writes no TCB word below 224 and no
thread's bound-VCPU / `RUN_VCPU` word. Main result: `K8.fin_thread.blk` (the thread kind with no bound VCPU and no
run in flight: `BlkOK` and a `K8.FootD` footprint). New definitions and theorems only; no existing statement
changed; no named premise.
